        'For a beam with fck=20 N/mm² and fy=415 N/mm², the design strengths are fcd=0.67×20/1.5≈8.9 N/mm² and fyd=415/1.15=361 N/mm². The factored load on a member with dead load 10 kN/m and live load 5 kN/m is 1.5×(10+5)=22.5 kN/m.',
        'State the characteristic and design values with the factors used; the examiner awards marks for the factored load and design strengths separately.',
        'In limit state design, the partial safety factor applied to the characteristic strength of steel is commonly taken as',
